# Trendza — Cursor Rules (enforced)

## Scope
- Rebrand to Trendza; deprecate OutfitGrader AI branding.
- Build three pillars: color-analysis, closet, product-search.
- All new data in `trendza_*` tables; legacy tables read-only where needed.
 - Replace purple/blue/orange UI with clean white background and black foreground.

## Architecture
- AI calls run only via Supabase Edge Functions.
- Use Nebius Mistral model for image/LLM tasks.
- RLS mandatory on all user data tables.
 - Feature flags must guard all new pillars; no breaking existing flows until flag removed.
 - Rate limit Edge Functions; set 30s timeout default; return typed JSON contracts.

## Code Standards
- TypeScript: strict, no `any` in new code.
- Verb-based function names; descriptive variables.
- Early returns; shallow control flow.
- No TODO comments; implement or track.
 - Error handling: never swallow; log with context and user-safe messages.

## Directories
- src/features/{color,closet,search}
- src/design for tokens/components
- supabase/functions/{color-analysis,closet-tagger,product-search}
- supabase/migrations/*trendza*

## UI/Design
- Base: white background, black text.
- Accent: #111111 text, #0A84FF minimal accent.
- Use tokens in `src/design/tokens.ts` (to be added).
 - Typography: system stack; sizes via tokens only.
 - Spacing via tokens; no hard-coded px beyond tokens.
 - Components must support light mode (default). No gradients.

## Security
- Media stored in user-prefixed folders.
- No client-stored API secrets.
- Logs must not contain PII.
 - Enforce RLS policies for all `trendza_*` tables (select/insert/update/delete by owner); products table read-only if global.

## Testing/CI
- Lint + typecheck gate.
- Contract tests for Edge Functions.
- Minimal E2E for core flows.
 - Snapshot tests for tokens and design primitives.

## Naming
- Tables: `trendza_*`.
- Functions: `color-analysis`, `closet-tagger`, `product-search`.

## Migration Rules
- Migrations must be idempotent and additive.
- Policies defined alongside tables.
 
## Pillar Rules
- Color Analysis:
  - Input: selfie base64 or public URL; Output: { undertone, season, palette[], faceMetrics }
  - Store in `trendza_color_profiles` (upsert by user_id)
  - Provide shareable summary string (no PII)
- Closet:
  - Input: item image → tags + attributes; save `trendza_closet_items`
  - Outfit generation returns item_ids[], score, rationale; save `trendza_outfits`
- Product Search:
  - Input: query + filters; Output: array of normalized products with price, brand, url
  - Cache minimal product snapshots in `trendza_products`; do not store affiliate secrets

## Analytics
- Track: color_analysis_completed, closet_item_added, outfit_generated, product_clicked
- No 3rd-party identifiers in logs; respect user consent flags.

