## Benchmark UX Principles (enforced)
- From Fitted ([App Store](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/fitted/id6596771952)):
  - Top-level closet tabs: `Pieces`, `Fits`, `Collections`.
  - Chip filters row (favorites, type, size, brand, color, season).
  - Each piece shows attributes (brand, type, color, season).
  - Outfit generator supports per-slot lock/swap; save named fits to collections.
  - Display a lightweight closet value/credit indicator in the header when relevant.
- From Style DNA ([App Store](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/style-dna-ai-color-analysis/id1358319821?mt=8)):
  - Selfie-first onboarding → undertone/season output → palette.
  - "Does this match me?" item checks with factors (color/shape/print/fabric) and clear pass indicator.
  - AI stylist chat entry near results; wardrobe and shopping tabs remain accessible.
- From Phia ([App Store](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/phia-best-price-in-one-click/id6739351340?fbclid=PAZXh0bgNhZW0CMTEAAae8kSz2inpK1Tncf0U6Armc7CftFsxrqN3BKWaa3QMzXBOXXGAJkt601Oc_CQ_aem_5j1BM7zMWsdMQfWyXZoH1Q)):
  - Instant price comparisons with a deal score bar; partner marketplace tiles on results.
  - Home shows trending searches and "Top deals from your brands".
  - Normalized product cards with external deep links.

## Pillar Feature Minimums (derived from benchmarks)
- Color Analysis: selfie → undertone/season → palette; item match API; shareable result.
- Closet: auto-tag upload; chip filters (favorites/type/size/brand/color/season); outfit generator with lock/swap; collections grid; closet value metric.
- Search: query + filters → normalized results; deal score bar; partner badges; external links; optional cached snapshot.

## UI Composition Rules (derived from screenshots)
- Large, left-aligned headlines; generous whitespace; avoid heavy gradients.
- Card lists with subtle shadows from `tokens.shadow`; rounded corners via `radii`.
- Bottom navigation with 4–5 tabs; persistent search icon on shopping screens.
- Chips with clear selected state; use accent color sparingly.


